        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "I am afraid I am going to close this as \"won't fix\". For at least these reasons:\r\n- The whole Operator-pending mode mapping situation is rather convoluted and limited to what Vim provides (from which Neovim \"inherits\" this part of code base).\r\n- The [official suggestion](https://neovim.io/doc/user/map.html#omap-info) as to how make a textobject (selection which ignores starting cursor position) also doesn't preserve previous visual selection. You can try this with `vim.cmd('onoremap <silent> F :<C-U>normal! 0f(hviw<CR>')` (assuming 'mini.jump' is not loaded afterwards) and `yF` for in line `aa bb(cc)`.\r\n- I tried several approaches of \"save and restore\" marks for previous visual selection, but none of them worked. The reason seems to be that the actual change of those marks happens [*after* the `<Cmd>...<CR>` in expression mapping](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/10426fc5bd38397c9a74d80cd4a6c55243fc78de/lua/mini/ai.lua#L1265) is executed (after `<CR>` to be more precise). Modifying that returned `<Cmd>...<CR>` to save and restore (like `<Cmd>lua <save>; <select><CR><Cmd>lua <restore><CR>`) breaks mappings for some unknown reason.",
            "created_at": "2024-07-30T09:35:12Z",
